  "regression_evidence": [
    "A two-rule candidate is created and reviewed through the TUI action port, registered through actual local IPC, and used to admit a later recorded native session.",
    "The manual and configured-judge measurement contracts match their real scoring paths. Evaluator choice refreshes after a judge change.",
    "Registration preserves Off/Manual state; replaying an already committed registration after a mode change neither creates another experiment nor changes its generation.",
    "A changed mode or routing snapshot rejects an uncommitted preview. Re-review permits registration; changed preview content and foreign-owner previews are rejected.",
    "Overlapping matchers and unavailable candidate routes are rejected before registration; the catalog identifies existing matchers.",
    "Drafts survive coding-transport disconnection, reject a different native session and cannot coexist with a manual review draft. Discard creates no experiment.",
    "Balanced-account preview lists all configured accounts and request-format paths deterministically, identifies rotation and omits credentials and endpoint URLs.",
    "Exact JSON float round trips preserve the bit pattern and digest of default policy priors across IPC and persistence."
